[{:db/id 17592186133822 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-130f7ccc-d087-5052-915e-6df794e733bd" "question-4cb13173-852b-58a2-8c1f-3d6511a05fac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133634 :question/problem "![](images/71/7122f0c4dd74925137e301a4b0ac3672d1f1b30cadf19f3bce438bce202b5720.svg)\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a-b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as \n![](images/d4/d48e14c19cb4927af5d1199fe7a8f34ff4ddd96314f56d69534d438786dc2ff9.svg)\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}80 & -60 & -20 \\\\ -60 & 45 & 15 \\\\ -20 & 15 & 5\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}32 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na-b+c=(-20)-(-24)+(-20) = -16.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133610 :question/problem "![](images/16/169c756c5420efe2234b3f20da794cc77e45f24c27cfafadfdf899ea9330c986.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $\\mathbf{b}$ shown above. Find the general least-squares solution of the system $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\nA^T \\! A\\mathbf{x} = A^T\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 \\\\ -18 & 54\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the above matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -4 \\\\ -18 & 54 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & -18 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\nx_1=-\\dfrac{2}{3}+3x_2.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n![](images/8c/8c70b499e599314c309470a3a46b99ab3172774886aa08c5dccffac0f130721b.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133611 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. Find the general least-squares solution of the system $A \\mathbf x = \\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where \n\n![](images/9e/9e09cbd3d953c8ce24e0a4b8a2b37c90dc3fc00d20c008b64dd068737c6ff49e.svg)\n\nThe least-squares solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\nA^T \\! A\\mathbf{x} = A^T\\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nNotice that the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent. So first, let's write down the normal equation in matrix form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}9 & -36 \\\\ -36 & 144\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system corresponding to the final matrix equation using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -36 & 3 \\\\ -36 & 144 & -12\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & -36 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, $x_2$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we have \n\n$$\nx_1=\\dfrac{1}{3}+ 4x_2.\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n![](images/bb/bb44b493b7c78eb144467289be8a7eef6f56c65ae37efcd742475c1ac0a55690.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186269135 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-3\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & a & 10 \\\\ c & 80 & -20 \\\\ 10 & -20 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ b \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a-b+c?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186269134 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -6{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}40 & -20 & -60 \\\\ -20 & 10 & a \\\\ c & 30 & 90\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ b \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-130f7ccc-d087-5052-915e-6df794e733bd" :question/id #uuid "130f7ccc-d087-5052-915e-6df794e733bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-136921" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ above. If the normal equation corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+4=54.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d8116051-5575-52c2-b4e3-895e85818216"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d8116051-5575-52c2-b4e3-895e85818216" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8116051-5575-52c2-b4e3-895e85818216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20388d9f-ef78-593d-a86d-57d7b9255118" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75f256ad-47a3-5c49-a78e-1c5ae0257228" "answer-6235969c-cd1d-5e61-9e7a-9328ddcaeab8" "answer-20388d9f-ef78-593d-a86d-57d7b9255118" "answer-903e90ec-6c0f-5989-8ade-87db319935c6" "answer-adae751b-b0cd-56eb-9595-ed2b595298d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75f256ad-47a3-5c49-a78e-1c5ae0257228" :answer/id #uuid "75f256ad-47a3-5c49-a78e-1c5ae0257228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6235969c-cd1d-5e61-9e7a-9328ddcaeab8" :answer/id #uuid "6235969c-cd1d-5e61-9e7a-9328ddcaeab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20388d9f-ef78-593d-a86d-57d7b9255118" :answer/id #uuid "20388d9f-ef78-593d-a86d-57d7b9255118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-903e90ec-6c0f-5989-8ade-87db319935c6" :answer/id #uuid "903e90ec-6c0f-5989-8ade-87db319935c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-adae751b-b0cd-56eb-9595-ed2b595298d5" :answer/id #uuid "adae751b-b0cd-56eb-9595-ed2b595298d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "62" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4cb13173-852b-58a2-8c1f-3d6511a05fac" :question/id #uuid "4cb13173-852b-58a2-8c1f-3d6511a05fac" :question/math-academy-id "q-136920" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & a \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ c & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+4+10=24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-389ee680-9312-52e5-a68e-aecf86a358ef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-389ee680-9312-52e5-a68e-aecf86a358ef" :answer-field/id #uuid "389ee680-9312-52e5-a68e-aecf86a358ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d4b6a212-c60d-5b71-a8fe-b61548150715" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06a52bea-6ee1-5ba3-91a9-fa2c837b2777" "answer-a4dbc700-783c-5f48-a597-56c6ebf71f61" "answer-d4b6a212-c60d-5b71-a8fe-b61548150715" "answer-8612d6bf-1d46-5e5b-bb7f-ca4d007e7546" "answer-1c6dd795-91e5-55e1-984a-5549435634d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06a52bea-6ee1-5ba3-91a9-fa2c837b2777" :answer/id #uuid "06a52bea-6ee1-5ba3-91a9-fa2c837b2777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4dbc700-783c-5f48-a597-56c6ebf71f61" :answer/id #uuid "a4dbc700-783c-5f48-a597-56c6ebf71f61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4b6a212-c60d-5b71-a8fe-b61548150715" :answer/id #uuid "d4b6a212-c60d-5b71-a8fe-b61548150715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8612d6bf-1d46-5e5b-bb7f-ca4d007e7546" :answer/id #uuid "8612d6bf-1d46-5e5b-bb7f-ca4d007e7546" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c6dd795-91e5-55e1-984a-5549435634d1" :answer/id #uuid "1c6dd795-91e5-55e1-984a-5549435634d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186269137 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $2a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415139 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $12a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186367450 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $5a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186269140 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $-9a+\\frac{b}{c}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415141 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations shown above. If the general least-squares solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $6a+\\frac{4b}{c}?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135060 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the following inconsistent system of equations:\n\n![](images/6b/6bcdc34077d88eac5ed89d408a1d2525b617a4f427b13433757df918585d380f.svg)\n\nSince the system is inconsistent, we cannot find an exact solution. However, as we've previously seen, we can attempt to find the so-called least-squares solution, which is a vector ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\|  A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\|\n$$\n\nis as small as possible. \n\nAs before, the least-squares solution can be found by solving the corresponding normal equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, note the following: \n\n- Previously, we solved the normal equation by left-multiplying the normal equation by $(A^T A)^{-1}.$\n\n- However, in this case, the second column of $A$ is a multiple of the first.\n\n- So, the columns of $A$ are linearly dependent.\n\n- Therefore, $A^T A$ is not invertible.\n\nTo solve the normal equation in this case, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5 & -20 \\\\ -20 & 80\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the last equation by Gaussian elimination, we obtain the general solution\n\n![](images/b9/b93bd5cb988f208eb26115bfaa08e81be989ee79cf3655612c1a0522a5566d95.svg)\n\nNotice that our solution is not unique! The second term of the least-squares solution (highlighted in blue) represents vectors from the null space of $A.$ \n\nIn general, if a matrix $A$ has collinear columns, then the least-squares solution to $A\\mathbf x = \\mathbf b$ is not unique." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134027 :activity/expected-seconds 1200.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
